WEBVTT

00:00.840 --> 00:05.900
Let's say that we have
a sheet of cardboard

00:05.900 --> 00:08.620
that is 20 inches by 30 inches.

00:08.620 --> 00:11.535
Let me draw the cardboard
as neatly as I can.

00:11.535 --> 00:13.810
So it might look
something like that.

00:13.810 --> 00:16.846
So that is my
sheet of cardboard.

00:16.846 --> 00:18.720
And just to make sure
we know the dimensions,

00:18.720 --> 00:22.150
there's 20 inches by 30 inches.

00:22.150 --> 00:24.240
And what we're
going to do is cut

00:24.240 --> 00:26.050
out the corners
of this cardboard.

00:26.050 --> 00:28.960
And all the corners are
going to be squares,

00:28.960 --> 00:31.870
and we're going to cut
out an x by x corner

00:31.870 --> 00:39.380
from each of the corners of this
piece of cardboard-- x by x.

00:39.380 --> 00:46.034
Over here, x by x, and
then over here, x by x.

00:46.034 --> 00:48.200
And what we'll do is after
we cut out those corners,

00:48.200 --> 00:51.260
we can essentially
fold down the flaps.

00:51.260 --> 00:52.240
Let me draw the flap.

00:52.240 --> 00:54.740
So you could imagine we
can fold right there,

00:54.740 --> 00:58.210
we could fold right there,
we could fold right there,

00:58.210 --> 00:59.600
and we would form a box.

00:59.600 --> 01:02.950
I guess you could imagine a
box without a bottom to it,

01:02.950 --> 01:05.170
or you can view a box
without a top to it.

01:05.170 --> 01:07.130
So if we were to
fold everything up,

01:07.130 --> 01:10.490
we would get a container that
looks something like this.

01:10.490 --> 01:12.770
Let me make my best
attempt to draw it.

01:12.770 --> 01:15.340
So it would look like this.

01:18.250 --> 01:20.500
This is one flap folded up.

01:20.500 --> 01:22.920
You can imagine this
flap right over here,

01:22.920 --> 01:25.170
if I were to fold
it up like that,

01:25.170 --> 01:28.230
it now would look like this.

01:28.230 --> 01:29.580
It would now look like this.

01:29.580 --> 01:32.190
The height of the flap is x.

01:32.190 --> 01:36.180
So this distance
right over here is x.

01:36.180 --> 01:39.690
And then if I were to fold
this flap, if I were-- let

01:39.690 --> 01:41.920
me do that a little bit neater.

01:41.920 --> 01:44.460
If I were to fold this
flap right over here,

01:44.460 --> 01:47.735
if I were to fold that up,
then it would look like this.

01:50.250 --> 01:53.420
Let me make my best
attempt to draw it.

01:53.420 --> 01:57.970
It would look like that.

01:57.970 --> 02:01.460
And then I would fold
that back flap up.

02:01.460 --> 02:05.896
So the back flap would
look something like that.

02:05.896 --> 02:08.690
That would be the back flap.

02:08.690 --> 02:10.690
It would look
something like that.

02:10.690 --> 02:12.940
And then this flap
over here would--

02:12.940 --> 02:19.930
if I fold it up would
look something like that.

02:19.930 --> 02:22.620
And then of course, my
base of my whole thing,

02:22.620 --> 02:26.590
so this whole region right over
here of my piece of cardboard,

02:26.590 --> 02:31.300
would be the floor of this
box that I'm constructing.

02:31.300 --> 02:33.530
And what I want to do
is I want to maximize

02:33.530 --> 02:35.240
the volume of this box.

02:35.240 --> 02:37.840
I want to maximize
how much it can hold.

02:37.840 --> 02:41.980
And I want to maximize it by
picking my x appropriately.

02:41.980 --> 02:44.540
So let's think about what
the volume of this box

02:44.540 --> 02:45.784
is as a function of x.

02:45.784 --> 02:47.200
Well, in order to
do that, we have

02:47.200 --> 02:51.620
to figure out all the dimensions
of this box as a function of x.

02:51.620 --> 02:54.600
We already know that this
corner right over here,

02:54.600 --> 02:57.510
which is made up of when
this side and this side

02:57.510 --> 02:59.684
connect when you fold
these two flaps up,

02:59.684 --> 03:01.600
that's going to be the
same height over there.

03:01.600 --> 03:03.516
That's going to be the
same height over there.

03:03.516 --> 03:05.770
The height of this
box is going to be x.

03:05.770 --> 03:07.490
But what's the width?

03:07.490 --> 03:11.672
What is the width of
this box going to be?

03:11.672 --> 03:13.130
Well, the width of
the box is going

03:13.130 --> 03:16.440
to be this distance
right over here.

03:16.440 --> 03:21.970
And this distance is going
to be 20 inches minus not 1x,

03:21.970 --> 03:23.930
but minus 2 x's.

03:23.930 --> 03:27.285
So this is going
to be 20 minus 2x.

03:27.285 --> 03:28.410
You see it right over here.

03:28.410 --> 03:30.030
This whole distance is 20.

03:30.030 --> 03:31.990
You subtract this x,
you subtract this x,

03:31.990 --> 03:34.370
and you get this
distance right over here.

03:34.370 --> 03:36.670
So it's 20 minus 2x.

03:36.670 --> 03:41.260
Now, the same logic, what
is the depth of the box?

03:41.260 --> 03:44.990
What is that distance
right over there?

03:44.990 --> 03:50.030
Well, that distance is this
distance right over here.

03:50.030 --> 03:53.090
We know that this entire
distance is 30 inches.

03:53.090 --> 03:56.870
If we subtract out this x
and we subtract out this x,

03:56.870 --> 03:58.910
we get the distance
that we care about.

03:58.910 --> 04:04.280
So this is going
to be 30 minus 2x.

04:04.280 --> 04:06.420
So now we have all
of the dimensions.

04:06.420 --> 04:09.850
So what would the volume
be as a function of x?

04:09.850 --> 04:14.120
Well, the volume
as a function of x

04:14.120 --> 04:16.490
is going to be equal
to the height, which

04:16.490 --> 04:24.430
is x, times the width, which
is 20 minus x-- sorry, 20

04:24.430 --> 04:28.230
minus 2x times the depth,
which is 30 minus 2x.

04:32.500 --> 04:37.460
Now, what are possible values of
x that give us a valid volume?

04:37.460 --> 04:41.390
Well, x can't be less than 0.

04:41.390 --> 04:42.970
You can't make a
negative cut here.

04:42.970 --> 04:45.780
Somehow we would have to add
cardboard or something there.

04:45.780 --> 04:48.680
So we know that x is going to
be greater than or equal to 0.

04:48.680 --> 04:50.370
So let me write this down.

04:50.370 --> 04:54.440
x is going to be greater
than or equal to 0.

04:54.440 --> 04:56.700
And what does it
have to be less than?

04:56.700 --> 04:59.270
Well, I can cut at
most-- we can see here

04:59.270 --> 05:02.270
the length right over here, this
pink color, this mauve color,

05:02.270 --> 05:04.330
is 20 minus 2x.

05:04.330 --> 05:06.170
So this has got to
be greater than 0.

05:06.170 --> 05:09.200
This is always going to be
shorter than the 30 minus 2x,

05:09.200 --> 05:15.460
but the 20 minus 2x has to be
greater than or equal to 0.

05:15.460 --> 05:17.870
You can't cut more
cardboard than there is.

05:17.870 --> 05:21.720
Or you could say that 20 has to
be greater than or equal to 2x,

05:21.720 --> 05:24.720
or you could say
that 10 is going

05:24.720 --> 05:26.910
to be greater than
or equal to x, which

05:26.910 --> 05:30.510
is another way of saying that
x is going to be less than

05:30.510 --> 05:32.570
or equal to 10.

05:32.570 --> 05:34.190
That's a different
shade of yellow.

05:34.190 --> 05:36.950
x is going to be less
than or equal to 10.

05:36.950 --> 05:39.800
So x has got to be
between 0 and 10.

05:39.800 --> 05:42.850
Otherwise we've cut too
much, or we're somehow

05:42.850 --> 05:44.940
adding cardboard or something.

05:44.940 --> 05:49.430
So first let's think about
the volume at the endpoints

05:49.430 --> 05:51.860
of our-- essentially of
our domain, of what x

05:51.860 --> 05:53.860
can be for our volume.

05:53.860 --> 05:59.670
Well, our volume when x is
equal to 0 is equal to what?

05:59.670 --> 06:01.331
We can have 0 times
all of this stuff.

06:01.331 --> 06:02.330
And it's pretty obvious.

06:02.330 --> 06:04.060
You're not going to
have any height here.

06:04.060 --> 06:05.684
So you're not going
to have any volume,

06:05.684 --> 06:07.440
so our volume would be 0.

06:07.440 --> 06:11.120
What is our volume
when x is equal to 10?

06:11.120 --> 06:15.060
Well, if x equaled 10,
then the width here

06:15.060 --> 06:17.820
that I've drawn in
pink would be 0.

06:17.820 --> 06:19.984
So once again, we
would have no volume.

06:19.984 --> 06:22.025
And this term right over
here, if we just look at

06:22.025 --> 06:23.870
it algebraically would
also be, equal to 0,

06:23.870 --> 06:26.150
so this whole thing
would be equal to 0.

06:26.150 --> 06:29.160
So someplace in between
x equals 0 and x equals

06:29.160 --> 06:34.080
10 we should achieve
our maximum volume.

06:34.080 --> 06:37.120
And before we do it analytically
with a bit of calculus,

06:37.120 --> 06:38.150
let's do it graphically.

06:38.150 --> 06:41.100
So I'll get my handy TI-85 out.

06:41.100 --> 06:43.600
So let me get my TI-85 out.

06:43.600 --> 06:47.140
And so first let me set
my range appropriately

06:47.140 --> 06:48.460
before I attempt to graph it.

06:48.460 --> 06:50.260
So I'll put my graph function.

06:50.260 --> 06:51.910
Let me set my range.

06:51.910 --> 06:53.990
So my minimum x-value,
let me make that 0.

06:53.990 --> 06:55.980
We know that x cannot
be less than 0.

06:55.980 --> 07:00.190
My maximum x-value, well,
10 seems pretty good.

07:00.190 --> 07:01.980
My minimum y-value,
this is essentially

07:01.980 --> 07:03.100
going to be my volume.

07:03.100 --> 07:04.683
I'm not going to
have negative volume,

07:04.683 --> 07:06.500
so let me set that equal 0.

07:06.500 --> 07:08.320
And my maximum
y-value, let's see

07:08.320 --> 07:10.050
what would be reasonable here.

07:10.050 --> 07:12.010
I'm just going to
pick some a random x

07:12.010 --> 07:13.720
and see what type
of a volume I get.

07:13.720 --> 07:19.540
So if x were to be 5, it
would be 5 times 20 minus 10,

07:19.540 --> 07:21.650
which is 10.

07:21.650 --> 07:23.340
So that would be--
did I do that right?

07:23.340 --> 07:25.320
Yeah, 20 minus 2
times 5, so that

07:25.320 --> 07:28.620
would be 10, and then times
30 minus 2 times 5, which

07:28.620 --> 07:29.740
would be 20.

07:29.740 --> 07:33.560
So it would be 5
times 10 times 20.

07:33.560 --> 07:36.300
So you'd get a volume
of 1,000 cubic inches.

07:36.300 --> 07:38.510
And I just randomly
picked the number 5.

07:38.510 --> 07:41.960
So let me give my maximum
y-value a little higher

07:41.960 --> 07:44.300
than that just in case to
that isn't the maximum value.

07:44.300 --> 07:45.466
I just randomly picked that.

07:45.466 --> 07:48.610
So let's say yMax is 1,500,
and if for whatever reason

07:48.610 --> 07:50.330
our graph doesn't
fit in there, then

07:50.330 --> 07:53.290
maybe we can make
our yMax even larger.

07:53.290 --> 07:55.980
So I think this is going
to be a decent range.

07:55.980 --> 07:58.170
Now let's actually input
the function itself.

07:58.170 --> 08:02.250
So our volume is
equal to x times 20

08:02.250 --> 08:08.930
minus 2x minus 2x
times 30 minus 2x.

08:12.870 --> 08:14.990
And that looks about right.

08:14.990 --> 08:16.620
So now I think we can graph it.

08:16.620 --> 08:19.000
So 2nd, and I want to
select that up there,

08:19.000 --> 08:21.040
so I'll do Graph.

08:21.040 --> 08:25.580
And it looks like we
did get the right range.

08:25.580 --> 08:28.720
So this tells us volume is a
function of x between x is 0

08:28.720 --> 08:31.730
and x is 10, and it does look
like we hit a maximum point

08:31.730 --> 08:33.000
right around there.

08:33.000 --> 08:33.696
So what I'm going
to do is I'm going

08:33.696 --> 08:35.950
to use the Trace function
to figure out roughly

08:35.950 --> 08:37.360
what that maximum point is.

08:37.360 --> 08:39.559
So let me trace this function.

08:39.559 --> 08:41.070
So I can still go
higher, higher.

08:41.070 --> 08:41.570
OK.

08:41.570 --> 08:45.490
So over there my
volume is 1,055.5.

08:45.490 --> 08:48.990
Then I can get to 1,056.

08:48.990 --> 08:54.930
So let's see, this was
1,056.20, this is 1,056.24,

08:54.930 --> 08:57.060
then I go back to 1,055.

08:57.060 --> 08:59.950
So at least based
on the level of zoom

08:59.950 --> 09:01.450
that I have my
calculator right now,

09:01.450 --> 09:03.760
this is a pretty
good approximation

09:03.760 --> 09:07.650
for the maximum value that my
function actually takes on.

09:07.650 --> 09:10.530
So it looks like my maximum
value is around 1,056,

09:10.530 --> 09:15.110
and it happens at
around x equals 3.89.

09:15.110 --> 09:23.020
So it looks like
my volume at 3.89

09:23.020 --> 09:28.630
is approximately equal
to 1,056 cubic inches.

09:28.630 --> 09:33.010
Or you could say that
we hit a maximum when

09:33.010 --> 09:39.150
x is approximately
equal to 3.89.

09:39.150 --> 09:41.880
So far, we've just set up
our maximization problem,

09:41.880 --> 09:44.480
and we've looked
at it graphically.

09:44.480 --> 09:46.930
In the next video, we'll
try to solve it analytically

09:46.930 --> 09:49.870
using some of our
calculus tools.
